  "prediction_locks": {
    "mission_1.route": {
      "context_signature": "09ef949f5d712b72",
      "text": "Go forward then turn to enter the door way then go right then right again to get to the bottom right room go forward so it can map out the walls then turn back then go to y=5 then go left when it sees a wall then go down. When it see a wall then turn around and get out of the room then go down and go right to get to the left side of the house when it reaches a wall turn right then if there is an opening on the left side turn left then go down. It might not cover all the walls since the LiDAR might not reach it to map all the walls."
    },
    "mission_2.strategy": {
      "context_signature": "b3281028443087d3",
      "text": "I will make this route try to explore more so it have less unknown areas. It should produce a clearer map because it will go to areas that it did not explore before."
    }
  },
  "responses": {
    "mission_1.drift_and_revisit": "The walls near the entrance is shifted and some are doubled. The left side of the entrance seems like there is 2 walls and there are some LiDAR that detected it is a free space. The right side of the entrance it already saw that it is free space but there is an extra wall that blocks the free space.",
    "mission_1.limitations": "Under the table on the right side of the house. When going through the area, the robot did not go close enough to the area to see what is there. The middle left of the house is the place where the route did not go to so it is too far for the sensors to detect. ",
    "mission_1.route.original_prediction": "Go forward then turn to enter the door way then go right then right again to get to the bottom right room go forward so it can map out the walls then turn back then go to y=5 then go left when it sees a wall then go down. When it see a wall then turn around and get out of the room then go down and go right to get to the left side of the house when it reaches a wall turn right then if there is an opening on the left side turn left then go down. It might not cover all the walls since the LiDAR might not reach it to map all the walls.",
    "mission_1.route.prediction_draft": "It should go to every room. It will revisit the places where it has to go to get to another room and when it goes inside a room it has to go back out. It might not map out places that are too far away from it.",
    "mission_2.comparison": "The first strategy since it has more known area per minute of 10.71 compared to 5.08 for strategy 2. Strategy 2 has more known fraction but it took a lot longer to map out while strategy 1 has fast but some areas are not mapped.",
    "mission_2.map_choice": "I would trust strategy 1 more because for strategy 2, 2 of the legs of the table on the left side of the house is inside of one of the other rooms.  Strategy 1 mapped less of the area with know area of 85.7 m^2  but is more accurate because it has a quality score of 84.8. Strategy 2 has mapped with 91.36 m^2 more but less accurate with quality score of 82.3.",
    "mission_2.strategy.original_prediction": "I will make this route try to explore more so it have less unknown areas. It should produce a clearer map because it will go to areas that it did not explore before.",
